+// 64-bit PowerPC, little-endian, ELFv2 ("ppc64le"), POWER8 (ISA 2.07) floor.
+//
+// Normative: flutter-port/work/abi/ABI-SPEC.md (section numbers below refer
+// to it) and work/abi/assembler_ppc64_api.h, whose declarations this header
+// contains verbatim or as source-compatible supersets (see "Freeze notes").
+//
+// Layers:
+//   L0  constants_ppc64.h   instruction words, field encoders, predicates.
+//   L1  MicroAssembler      one raw emitter per PPC64_INSTRUCTION_LIST entry
+//                           plus the extended mnemonics, inline between the
+//                           BEGIN/END L1 RAW EMITTERS markers below. The
+//                           encoding oracle lifts that region verbatim.
+//   L2  Assembler           DS-safe memory access, immediates, labels and
+//                           branches, the deferred compare, calls, frames.
+//   L3  Assembler           the AssemblerBase virtuals and everything shared
+//                           code calls.
+//
+// Rules every method obeys (ABI-SPEC sections 1, 2.2, 11):
+//   R1. R0 may be clobbered by any L2/L3 method and by nothing in L1. No value
+//       is live in R0 across an L2/L3 call.
+//   R2. TMP (R11) and TMP2 (R12) are clobbered only where a comment says so.
+//   R3. No L1 emitter accepts R0 as the (RA|0) operand of a storage access,
+//       addi, addis or isel; no emitter accepts R2 or R13 anywhere; no
+//       emitter writes CR2..CR4. These are RELEASE_ASSERTs: each violation
+//       would be a silent miscompile, so they hold in release builds too.
+//   R4. CR0 and CR7 are dead across every L2/L3 call. L2/L3 write no other CR
+//       field; CR1, CR5 and CR6 are free for hand-written sequences.
+//   R5. Nothing is ever stored below R1.
+//
+// Where each out-of-line method is defined (the ownership contract for the
+// three .cc files; WORK-SPLIT.md section 3). Every method declared without a
+// body below carries exactly one of these tags:
+//   [core]  assembler_ppc64.cc       Agent A, phase 1. Standalone (tier 2).
+//   [ext]   assembler_ppc64_ext.cc   Agent B, phase 1. Standalone (tier 2).
+//   [vm-A]  assembler_ppc64_vm.cc    Agent A, phase 2. Needs the VM.
+//   [vm-B]  assembler_ppc64_vm.cc    Agent B, phase 2. Needs the VM.
+//   [none]  assembler_ppc64_vm.cc    UNIMPLEMENTED() for good (no TSAN on
+//                                    ppc64); never reached.
+// [core] and [ext] bodies call only L1, [core], [ext] and inline methods, so
+// that both files link without the VM. Bodies in this header are limited to
+// L1, the buffer primitives, accessors, pure forwards to a declared method,
+// and the template-identical UNREACHABLE()s for unsupported SIMD.
+
+namespace dart {
+
+// Forward declarations.
+class FlowGraphCompiler;
+class RuntimeEntry;
+class RegisterSet;
